From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] EE scheduler: late VBlanks leave no debt to catch up

What it broke:
  A VBlank is due when the EE has run its cycles AND the host clock has
  reached its host deadline; each VBlank's host deadline was the previous
  one's plus 16.667 ms. When the game ran slower than real time, the host
  deadlines fell into the past, and when it later ran fast enough, the
  VBlanks came as soon as the EE cycles allowed until the chain had caught
  up with the clock: in a 20-minute Windows session of Protector of Earth
  Recomp the first level fell 86 s behind real time, and the loading and
  the second level then ran with up to 104 VBlanks per second (the game up
  to 1.7 times too fast) for several minutes.

The changes:
  - EeScheduler::processDueDeadlines: the next VBlank's host deadline is
    one period after max(this VBlank's host deadline, now - one period),
    so it is never before now. A game that falls behind runs in slow
    motion while it is slow and at 60 VBlanks per second again as soon as
    it can, with no fast stretch afterwards. The EE cycle at which each
    VBlank falls is unchanged.

How it was checked:
  Linux: the game reaches the first level; with BEN10_FPS_LOG=1 no second
  has more than 61 VBlanks (findings/20 s.43). ps2xTest 454/454.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/EeScheduler.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/EeScheduler.cpp
@@ -1885,11 +1885,19 @@
         {
             if (scheduled.event.type == EeEventType::VBlankStart)
             {
+                // The next VBlank is due one period after this one's host
+                // time, but never before now: a VBlank that comes late (the
+                // game ran slower than real time) does not leave a debt the
+                // following ones pay back by coming faster than 60 per
+                // second. With the debt, a long slow stretch made the game
+                // run up to 1.7 times too fast afterwards to catch up.
+                const auto pacedNow = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+                const auto hostBase = std::max(scheduled.hostDeadline, pacedNow - kVBlankPeriod);
                 scheduleEvent(scheduled.deadlineCycle + kVBlankDurationCycles,
-                              scheduled.hostDeadline + kVBlankDuration,
+                              hostBase + kVBlankDuration,
                               EeEvent{EeEventType::VBlankEnd, 0, m_vsyncTick + 1u});
                 scheduleEvent(scheduled.deadlineCycle + kVBlankPeriodCycles,
-                              scheduled.hostDeadline + kVBlankPeriod,
+                              hostBase + kVBlankPeriod,
                               EeEvent{EeEventType::VBlankStart, 0, 0});
             }
             processEvent(scheduled.event);
